{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-q","content":"You stir sugar into warm water and it disappears. What kind of change is this?"},{"type":"button","id":"c1-a","label":"A reversible change","why":"Evaporating the water brings the sugar back, so dissolving is reversible.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"An irreversible change","why":"Pupils may think the sugar is destroyed, but it can be recovered.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-c","label":"The sugar turns into a new substance","why":"Pupils may confuse dissolving with burning, which makes a new substance.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
